[background arg="res://assets/Scene_Overlay.png" fade="0.0"]
join Foreground (Diner Counter Day) rightmost [z_index="1"]
join Dagger (Close Up) lefter
join Knightmare (Close Up) midleft
join Lizzy (Close Up) right [z_index="2" extra_data="show Eyes/Side"]
Lizzy: you two look right at home behind the counter.

Lizzy: maybe if you're well behaved my parents'll offer you a job.
Dagger: this is the only place in your diner that is completely hidden from the sun.
Knightmare: how much is the payment for a job such as the one in which you are describing?
Dagger: my lady,
Dagger: you aren't really considering...
Dagger: you would loath working in food service.
Knightmare: I am charting my path.
Knightmare: you don't know until you try.
Lizzy: I think our little heart to heart last night was a good influence on you Lady Knightmare.
Lizzy: the board games after probably helped too.
Knightmare: I was most intrigued by the catan game.
Knightmare: my victory was assured.
Dagger: I notice your parents are here.
Dagger: Have you talked them yet?
set {current_decision} = GameState.spoken_today["parents"]
if {current_decision} == true:
	if {Choices.C_5} == true:
		Lizzy: i tried explaining everything,
		Lizzy: but they seemed more confused than anything.
		Dagger: it might take them a while to fully understand.
		Lizzy: unfortunately we don't have a while.
		Dagger: i thought you believed there was something after the end of the episode.
		Lizzy: well,
		Lizzy: yes, i do,
		Lizzy: but...
		Lizzy: I'm going to treat this like my last day on earth.
		Dagger: what a novel idea.
		Dagger: maybe if I approached my immortality the same way,
		Dagger: things would be different.
	else:
		Lizzy: Yeah,
		Lizzy: but I didn't tell them anything.
		Dagger: that's a shame.
		Dagger: it feels cruel to hide that part of yourself.
		Lizzy: hey,
		Lizzy: mr I killed my brother when I couldn't handle the pressure of a conversation.
		Lizzy: It's not easy to be honest!
		Dagger: fair enough.
		VO: maybe that was a bit mean.
		Knightmare: yes.
		Knightmare: cut him down!
		VO: okay, if Lady Knightmare's cheering me on...
		VO: I know i've done something wrong.
		Lizzy: sorry.
		Lizzy: I just don't want to them to worry about stuff when, well,
		Lizzy: this could be our last day together.
		Dagger: it's easy for me to judge others when I myself have not been burdened with the task of confession.
		Dagger: you know your parents best.
else:
	Lizzy: I'm building up to it.
	Dagger: will you tell them what happened?
	Lizzy: I'm not sure.
	Lizzy: i don't know how I'd even begin to explain everything.
	Lizzy: plus, they don't even know about my werewolf stuff.
	Dagger: perhaps now would be the time to share that part of your life.
	VO: man,
	VO: i hate it when he's right.

label C1
if {choice} == 3.0:
	jump C1_after
else:
	jump C1_choices
label C1_choices
- [VO] I wonder if they want [br] to go to the school dance. | [if {Choices.C_1} == 0.0] [else="hide"]
	set {Choices.C_1} += 1.0
	Lizzy: are you two going to grad?
	Dagger: are we invited
	Lizzy: absolutely.
	Lizzy: i think it's going to be pretty wild.
	Knightmare: i would be honored to attend the festival.
	Lizzy: it's not really a festival...
	Lizzy: more like a themed dance.
	Knightmare: what is the theme?
	Lizzy: happily ever after or something.
	Knightmare: ew.
	Dagger: i like it.
	Dagger: it's romantic.
	Lizzy: of course you would.
	Dagger: should we wear a costume for the occasion?
	Lizzy: i guess, if you want.
	Knightmare: i have just the thing.
	jump C1
- [VO] How are they dealing with the[br] whole Lizzy Springs TV show thing? | [if {Choices.C_2} == 0.0] [else="hide"]
	set {Choices.C_2} += 1.0
	Lizzy: so you're totally fine with your life being a television show?
	Knightmare: completely.
	Dagger: I've come to accept it.
	Knightmare: co-running a theatre company
	Knightmare: five hundred of my very long years of life was dedicated to performing in a show.
	Knightmare: a professional actor is skilled at maintaining character.
	Lizzy: so you can't ever turn it off, i see.
	Dagger: i am just thankful to be included in your inner circle, elizabeth.
	Dagger: despite our sortit history.
	Lizzy: yeah, yeah,
	Lizzy: enough of that.
	jump C1

- [VO] it seems rude not to introduce [br] them to mom and dad. | [if {Choices.C_3} == 0.0] [else="hide"]
	set {Choices.C_3} += 1.0
	Lizzy: want to meet my mom and dad?
	Dagger: no thank you.
	Knightmare: i would love to engage your mother in combat to see if your natural strength has been passed on maternally.
	Lizzy: uh, actually,
	Lizzy: on second thought..
	VO: it's probably best if they stay far away from eachother.
	jump C1

label C1_after
Lizzy: well, I gotta go.
Dagger: see you shortly, Elizabeth.
Knightmare: show your enemies no mercy.
Lizzy: bye.
set {Choices.C_1} = 0
set {Choices.C_2} = 0
set {Choices.C_3} = 0
leave --All-- [animation="Fade Out Down"]
